{title: Come, Ye Disconsolate}
{artist: Thomas Moore & Samuel Webbe}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 69}

Verse 1
[F]Come, ye discon[Bb]solate, wher[F]e'er ye [C]languish;
[F]come to the [Dm]mercy seat, [Gm]fervently [C]kneel.
[F]Here bring your [Bb]wounded hearts, [F]here tell your [C]anguish —
[F]earth has no [Bb]sorrow that [C]heaven cannot [F]heal.

Verse 2
Joy of the desolate,
light of the straying,
Hope of the penitent,
fadeless and pure,
Here speaks the Comforter,
tenderly saying,
"Earth has no sorrow
that Heav'n cannot cure."

Verse 3
Here see the Bread of Life;
see waters flowing
Forth from the throne of God,
pure from above;
Come to the feast of love;
come, ever
knowing Earth
has no sorrow
but Heav'n can remove.
